---
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import SvgFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/SvgFigure.astro"
---

<IllustrationFigure>
  <SvgFigure
    name="light-fig"
    class="w-full"
    viewBox="0 0 420 260"
    title="A sweeping lighthouse beam"
    desc="Two light rays leave a lighthouse at slightly different angles and meet far-apart points on a distant wall. The spots can change position along the wall faster than light even though the individual rays travel outwards at light speed."
  >
    <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
      <path d="M370 30 V215" stroke-width="6" />
      <path d="M50 200 L370 70" stroke="var(--color-series-red)" stroke-width="4" />
      <path d="M50 200 L370 170" stroke="var(--color-series-blue)" stroke-width="4" />
      <path d="M370 70 V170" stroke-dasharray="6 6" stroke-width="4" />
    </g>
    <g fill="var(--color-series-gold)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
      <path d="M22 216 H78 L70 232 H30 Z" />
      <rect x="40" y="182" width="20" height="34" />
      <circle cx="50" cy="200" r="6" />
    </g>
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="18" font-family="sans-serif">
      <text x="50" y="254" text-anchor="middle">
        Lighthouse
      </text>
      <text x="360" y="40" text-anchor="end">
        Wall
      </text>
      <text x="380" y="78">
        A
      </text>
      <text x="380" y="178">
        B
      </text>
    </g>
  </SvgFigure>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    The wall receives separate rays, not a sideways-moving object. A moving patch of light is
    not a message travelling from point A to point B along the wall.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
